<sn><md>#### Orinoco

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-6

```text
Orinoco   → Venezuela → Atlantic Ocean
```

- It flows mainly through **Venezuela** and forms part of the **border between Venezuela and Colombia** before flowing into the Atlantic Ocean
- The **Angel Falls** and the Orinoco River are geographically connected through the river system of Venezuela.
- One of the **largest rivers** in South America. 
:::

:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
![img](https://www.shutterstock.com/shutterstock/photos/2685374017/display_1500/stock-vector-vector-map-of-the-orinoco-river-including-its-drainage-basin-and-its-main-tributaries-2685374017.jpg)
:::
:::
</md></sn><sn><md>### Magdelena River

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
![img](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Rio_Magdalena_map.png/500px-Rio_Magdalena_map.png?utm_source=hif.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail)
:::

:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
```
Magdalena → Colombia → Caribbean Sea
```

- The most important river of **Colombia**. 
- It flows northward through Colombia and empties into the **Caribbean Sea**.
- It is important for transportation and agriculture
:::
:::
